{
  "id": "COMPOUND:12639 - PROTEIN:367",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions where Umbralisib is linked to the S-methylmethionine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase BHMT2 through multiple intermediate targets. Specifically, Umbralisib is directly associated with Serine--tRNA ligase, cytoplasmic, which in turn is targeted by certolizumab pegol and by 13-[(2R,3R,4R)-3,4-dihydroxy-2-(hydroxymethyl)-3,4-dihydro-2H-pyrrol-5-yl]-1-hydroxytridecan-5-one. Both of these intermediates are also targeted by Umbralisib and ultimately lead to the BHMT2 enzyme. This indicates that Umbralisib may act through a series of molecular pathways that ultimately modulate BHMT2 activity. The high scores across all three paths suggest a strong and consistent relationship, but the exact mechanism by which Umbralisib influences BHMT2 remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a potential regulatory role of Umbralisib in BHMT2 function, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
